@startuml
title Anatomy of a page in this suite: the seven required parts, and what each one is answerable to

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #F9FAFB
  BorderColor #9CA3AF
}

rectangle "**THE SPECIFICATION**\n`languages/src/<lang>.rs`" as SPEC #F3F4F6 {
  rectangle "**name / types**\nthe sorts" as S_TYPES #DBEAFE
  rectangle "**terms**\nsignature <latex>\Sigma</latex>\n+ concrete syntax" as S_TERMS #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**equations**\ntheory <latex>E</latex>" as S_EQNS #FEF3C7
  rectangle "**rewrites**\nsystem <latex>R</latex>" as S_REWS #FCE7F3
}

rectangle "**THE PAGE**\n`docs/languages/<lang>.md`" as PAGE #F3F4F6 {
  rectangle "**1. Header**\nsubject file, audience,\nand the METHOD by which\nclaims were verified" as P_HEAD #E0E7FF
  rectangle "**2. Table of contents**\nworking in-document anchors" as P_TOC #E0E7FF
  rectangle "**3. Notation table**\nevery symbol, acronym and\nkey term, BEFORE first use" as P_NOTE #EDE9FE
  rectangle "**4. One section per block**\nin the order the macro parses them,\nwith a fragment-by-fragment table\nper rule form" as P_BLOCKS #DBEAFE
  rectangle "**5. The whole specification**\nthe <latex>(\Sigma, E, R)</latex> triple,\na TEST-PINNED cheat-sheet,\nand a worked reduction" as P_WHOLE #DCFCE7
  rectangle "**6. Provenance table**\nevery claim mapped to\n`file:line`" as P_PROV #FEF3C7
  rectangle "**7. Gotchas**\nthe misreadings the page\nexists to prevent" as P_GOTCHA #FEE2E2
  rectangle "**References**\nDOI-bearing citations\n+ in-repo companions" as P_REFS #EDE9FE
}

rectangle "**THE EVIDENCE**\nwhat a claim may point at" as EVID #F3F4F6 {
  rectangle "the DSL parser\n`ast/src/`" as E_PARSE #DBEAFE
  rectangle "the code generator\n`macros/src/gen/`" as E_GEN #EDE9FE
  rectangle "the GENERATED OUTPUT\n`target/generated/<lang>/`" as E_OUT #DCFCE7
  rectangle "a pinned test\n`languages/tests/`, `repl/tests/`" as E_TEST #FEF3C7
}

rectangle "**THE GATE**\n`docs/languages/validate.sh`\n17 mechanised checks" as GATE #FCE7F3

S_TYPES -right-> P_BLOCKS
S_TERMS -right-> P_BLOCKS
S_EQNS  -right-> P_BLOCKS
S_REWS  -right-> P_BLOCKS

P_HEAD   .down.> E_PARSE : declares the method
P_BLOCKS .down.> E_GEN   : what the macro emits
P_WHOLE  .down.> E_OUT   : what it emitted HERE
P_PROV   .down.> E_TEST  : and what pins it

PAGE -down-> GATE : must pass before it lands

note right of P_NOTE
  Mechanised: an all-caps token that is
  not an English word must be expanded
  at or before its first use.
end note

note right of P_WHOLE
  Mechanised: every algorithm appears as
  a captioned ""```pseudocode"" block
  (**Algorithm N (Name).**) followed by
  prose explaining its steps — Knuth's
  literate form, not a code dump.
end note

note bottom of GATE
  A guideline nobody checks is a guideline that silently rots.
  This suite already proved it: all four of lambda.md's SVGs sat
  on disk at ZERO BYTES while their .puml sources had real content.
  The check that catches it existed. It had never been run.
end note

@enduml
